    "text": "```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"\n    A Least Recently Used (LRU) cache implementation using OrderedDict.\n    \n    The cache maintains a fixed capacity. When the cache is full and a new item\n    is inserted, the least recently used item is evicted.\n    \n    Methods:\n        get(key): Retrieve the value for the given key. Returns -1 if not found.\n        put(key, value): Insert or update the value for the given key.\n    \n    Time Complexity:\n        - get: O(1) average case\n        - put: O(1) average case\n    \n    Space Complexity:\n        - O(capacity) for storing up to 'capacity' items.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the LRU cache with a given capacity.\n        \n        Args:\n            capacity: Maximum number of items the cache can hold.\n        \"\"\"\n        if capacity <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be a positive integer\")\n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.cache = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n",
